      "method": "v1.1.0 case-law rebuild: authorities selected per decision point, each opinion retrieved from CourtListener and read; holding and quote taken from the opinion text; independently re-verified before release. Previous keyword-matched Justia listings were removed.",
      "verified_date": "2026-09-20",
      "key_cases": [
        {
          "case_name": "In the Interest of S.E.",
          "citation": "527 S.W.3d 894 (Mo. Ct. App. 2017)",
          "court": "Missouri Court of Appeals",
          "year": 2017,
          "date_decided": "2017-09-12",
          "holding": "The court held that an intervening tribe has authority under ICWA to appeal a termination judgment, but affirmed the termination because the tribe's claims that the mother's consent was invalid under 25 U.S.C. section 1913 and that the expert was unqualified under section 1912(f) were raised for the first time on appeal and produced no manifest injustice.",
          "relevance": "ICWA's placement and evidentiary protections exist to prevent culturally based removal decisions, and this case shows how they are enforced — or lost — in Missouri practice.",
          "quote": "Having concluded that the Tribe has the authority to assert this appeal, we turn to the merits of the Tribe's claims.",
          "url": "https://www.courtlistener.com/opinion/5448997/in-the-interest-of-se/",
          "courtlistener_cluster_id": 5448997
        },
        {
          "case_name": "Mitchell v. Dakota County Social Services",
          "citation": "959 F.3d 887 (8th Cir. 2020)",
          "court": "United States Court of Appeals for the Eighth Circuit",
          "year": 2020,
          "date_decided": "2020-05-19",
          "holding": "The Eighth Circuit affirmed dismissal of the parent's and children's section 1983 claims, holding that reliance on allegations during a child-abuse investigation and unprofessional statements by a caseworker were not conscience-shocking, that the equal protection and conspiracy claims failed, and that although children have a fundamental right not to be unreasonably removed from their home, that Fourth Amendment claim was not preserved below.",
          "relevance": "The opinion addresses and rejects, on this record, an equal protection challenge to a county's removal practices, marking what such a claim requires.",
          "quote": "The children have a fundamental right not to be unreasonably removed from their home.",
          "url": "https://www.courtlistener.com/opinion/4754922/dwight-mitchell-v-dakota-county-social-services/",
          "courtlistener_cluster_id": 4754922
        },
        {
          "case_name": "Palmore v. Sidoti",
          "citation": "466 U.S. 429 (1984)",
          "court": "Supreme Court of the United States",
          "year": 1984,
          "date_decided": "1984-04-25",
          "holding": "The Court reversed, holding that the Equal Protection Clause forbids a court from removing a child from a fit natural parent's custody because of the racial composition of the parent's household, since the possible effects of private racial bias are not a permissible basis for a custody decision.",
          "relevance": "Palmore is the governing federal standard that a child-placement decision may not rest on race or on anticipated community reaction to a family's racial composition, and it is the authority a discrimination claim in a Missouri placement dispute starts from.",
          "quote": "Private biases may be outside the reach of the law, but the law cannot, directly or indirectly, give them effect.",
          "url": "https://www.courtlistener.com/opinion/111160/palmore-v-sidoti/",
          "courtlistener_cluster_id": 111160
        }
      ],
